From 548d67cb8f1cd5da599b6d71a4d0381823c4a93f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Rockefeller <alanrockefeller@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:55:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Site repeats: grow-only CLV, scaler and id-to-site
 buffers

corax_default_reallocate_repeats() freed and reallocated a node's CLV,
scaler and id-to-site buffers whenever the node's number of repeat classes
changed, which during SPR is on nearly every CLV update (~4% of a run in
malloc/free/memalign and the reallocation itself).

The default callback now keeps a buffer that is already large enough; the
capacities are tracked in two new arrays in corax_repeats_t. A tip CLV
replaced by corax_update_repeats_tips() and buffers replaced by the binary
loader are marked unknown, which falls back to the old reallocation.

Exactness: every user writes the first sites_to_alloc entries of these
buffers before reading them (the CLV kernels write the whole parent CLV and
fill the parent scaler, corax_update_repeats() the id-to-site table), so a
reused buffer yields the same values. A -DCORAX_REPEATS_POISON_TEST build
fills every reused buffer with NaN/junk; it produces byte-identical output.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/corax/core/partition.c |  2 +
 src/corax/core/repeats.c   | 79 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 src/corax/core/repeats.h   |  8 ++++
 src/corax/io/binary.c      |  4 ++
 4 files changed, 74 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

