From 9194319c0acbce89fa67552221fad6f6318005a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Rockefeller <alanrockefeller@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 06:02:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Site repeats: branch-free class identification

corax_update_repeats() runs on every CLV update and decides per site
whether its (left class, right class) pair is new. On real alignments that
is close to a coin flip -- a parent averages about half as many classes as
there are sites -- so the branch mispredicted constantly (6-10% of a run,
the larger share with FreeRate models, whose kernels do less work per
site).

The loop now writes the slot curr_id of toclean_buffer/id_site_buffer for
every site, advances curr_id only for a new pair, selects the id with a
mask (written as ?: gcc turns it back into the branch) and rewrites an
existing lookup entry with its own value.

Exactness: integer bookkeeping only; the ids, the first ids entries of both
buffers and the lookup table end up exactly as before (checked on 20000
random class layouts against the original loop). End-to-end output cannot
catch a renumbering -- the likelihood does not depend on the class
numbering -- hence the unit check.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/corax/core/repeats.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/corax/core/repeats.c b/src/corax/core/repeats.c
index aa59bd8..cecb826 100644
--- a/src/corax/core/repeats.c
+++ b/src/corax/core/repeats.c
@@ -355,17 +355,25 @@ CORAX_EXPORT void corax_update_repeats(corax_partition_t *      partition,
   else
   {
     // fill the parent repeats identifiers
+    // Branch-free: whether a (left, right) pair is new is close to a coin
+    // flip, so the branch mispredicted constantly. The slot curr_id of the
+    // two buffers is written for every site but only kept (curr_id advanced)
+    // for a new pair, and an existing entry of the lookup table is rewritten
+    // with its own value, so the results are the same as before.
+    unsigned int *lookup = repeats->lookup_buffer;
     for (s = 0; s < partition->sites; ++s)
     {
       unsigned int index_lookup = site_id_left[s] + site_id_right[s] * ids_left;
-      unsigned int id           = repeats->lookup_buffer[index_lookup];
-      if (EMPTY_ELEMENT == id)
-      {
-        toclean_buffer[curr_id]              = index_lookup;
-        id_site_buffer[curr_id]              = s;
-        id                                   = curr_id;
-        repeats->lookup_buffer[index_lookup] = curr_id++;
-      }
+      unsigned int id           = lookup[index_lookup];
+      unsigned int is_new       = (EMPTY_ELEMENT == id);
+      /* select with a mask: written as ?: the compiler turns it back into
+       * the unpredictable branch */
+      unsigned int new_mask     = 0u - is_new;
+      toclean_buffer[curr_id]   = index_lookup;
+      id_site_buffer[curr_id]   = s;
+      id                        = (curr_id & new_mask) | (id & ~new_mask);
+      lookup[index_lookup]      = id;
+      curr_id += is_new;
       site_id_parent[s] = id;
     }
     ids = curr_id;
-- 
