From 2292f9022a64bb80f035b042668ad18e0323963a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Rockefeller <alanrockefeller@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 06:02:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] AVX 4x4 CLV update (site repeats): matrix-vector products
 from columns

The 4-state kernels compute P*v as four row products followed by a 4x4
transpose-add (unpacklo/unpackhi, add, permute2f128/blend, add): six
shuffles per product vector, five of them on port 5, the only shuffle port
on Haswell/Broadwell. matvec_4x4_cols.h computes the same vector from the
columns of P with broadcast elements of v.

Exactness: element i of the row-wise result is
(p_i0*v0 + p_i1*v1) + (p_i2*v2 + p_i3*v3); the column form computes the same
four products and pairs the additions the same way. IEEE addition is
commutative, so the results are bitwise identical (signed zeros included).
The header also has the variants the other kernels need: products added to
a zeroed accumulator (canon(a)+canon(b) == canon(a+b) with canon(x)=x+0, so
one +0 on the finished sum suffices) and FMAs into a zeroed accumulator
(formed per product, since fma(a,b,0) keeps an underflowed -0).

corax_core_update_clv_repeatsbclv_4x4_avx(), the CLV update used for DNA
with site repeats (~22% of a run), uses it, processes two parent sites per
iteration sharing the column loads (each site still goes through the same
operations), and ANDs the per-site scaling compare masks in vector
registers instead of moving each one to an integer register.

A harness running the old and new kernel on 4000 random cases (1-8 rate
categories, all repeat layouts, no/per-site/per-rate scaling, zero, -0,
subnormal and negative matrix entries, one-hot and tiny CLVs) compares the
parent CLV and scalers bit for bit: all identical. 1.51x faster on a
realistic call (208 parent classes, 13 left classes, 4 categories).

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/corax/kernel/avx/core_clv_avx.c | 230 +++++++++++++++++-----------
 src/corax/kernel/matvec_4x4_cols.h  |  70 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 208 insertions(+), 92 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/corax/kernel/matvec_4x4_cols.h

diff --git a/src/corax/kernel/avx/core_clv_avx.c b/src/corax/kernel/avx/core_clv_avx.c
