From 236046f7ab195e1d037f8f1da059781539b23327 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Rockefeller <alanrockefeller@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 06:02:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] AVX2 branch-length derivatives: 4-state fast path

corax_core_likelihood_derivatives_avx2() (~20% of a run) had two problems
for DNA. It was load-bound -- per site and rate category four broadcasts of
the sumtable and four loads of the diagptable, which is the same for every
site -- and every fourth site waited on a dependent chain: scalar loads of
the four just-stored site vectors (a store-forwarding stall), a 4-wide
division and the accumulation.

The 4-state path now works in chunks of 64 sites: first every site's
(LH, 1st, 2nd derivative) terms, two adjacent sites at a time sharing the
diagptable vectors (pinned in registers: otherwise gcc folds each load into
both sites' FMAs), then the derivative steps of the chunk back to back,
with the four site vectors read whole and transposed in registers. The
invariant-site table is on the stack instead of an aligned allocation on
every Newton iteration (+I models).

Exactness: each site goes through exactly the operations of the one-site
loop in the same order; chunks are multiples of 4, so the groups for the
derivative step are the same, and they are accumulated in the same order;
the remainder loop is unchanged. Harness: 6000 random cases (4 and 20
states, odd and even site counts, invariant sites, unequal rate weights,
pattern weights): first and second derivative identical bit for bit.
~1.5x faster per call.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/corax/kernel/avx2/core_derivatives_avx2.c | 213 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 171 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/corax/kernel/avx2/core_derivatives_avx2.c b/src/corax/kernel/avx2/core_derivatives_avx2.c
index ebba3ce..c297a62 100644
--- a/src/corax/kernel/avx2/core_derivatives_avx2.c
+++ b/src/corax/kernel/avx2/core_derivatives_avx2.c
@@ -1536,6 +1536,52 @@ corax_core_update_sumtable_ti_avx2(unsigned int         states,
   return CORAX_SUCCESS;
 }
 
+/* Derivative step for 4 adjacent sites whose (LH, 1st, 2nd derivative)
+ * terms are stored at site_lk[0..15], 4 per site; pw points at the pattern
+ * weight of the first of the 4 sites. */
+static inline void derivatives_4sites_avx2(const double *      site_lk,
+                                           const unsigned int *pw,
+                                           __m256d             v_all1,
+                                           __m256d *           v_df,
+                                           __m256d *           v_ddf)
+{
+  /* v_termK = (site_lk[K], site_lk[4+K], site_lk[8+K], site_lk[12+K]):
+   * a 4x4 transpose of the four stored site vectors, read back whole
+   * (assembling them from scalar loads of just-stored vectors stalls on
+   * store forwarding) */
+  __m256d s0      = _mm256_load_pd(site_lk);
